combo-burst.prompt:
A sprite sheet for a game VFX artist: ONE impact burst for a PC rhythm game, frame by frame. Flat 2D geometric light on pure black (#000000).

LAYOUT: exactly 10 frames in a 5 x 2 grid of equal cells (5 across, 2 down), read left to right, top to bottom. NO grid lines, NO borders, NO numbers, NO text. The burst is centred on the same point in every cell and stays inside its cell with black around it; nothing touches a cell edge.

THE ANIMATION:
- frame 1: a compact white-gold four-point star flare at the centre;
- frames 2-4: a diamond-shaped shockwave expands from it, with sharp light shards and thin radial needles;
- frames 5-7: the outer diamond breaks into four-point glints and short arc streaks flying outward;
- frames 8-9: only micro sparkles drifting outward, fading;
- frame 10: almost dark, one or two last faint specks.

COLOUR: pale gold-white, core #fff3c4, edges #ffc44d. Crisp edges, soft glow. No smoky clouds, no fire, no objects, no letters.

cracks-sheet.prompt:
A sprite sheet for a game VFX artist: glass cracking frame by frame, for a PC rhythm game's track. Flat orthographic 2D, seen straight from the front, on pure black (#000000).

LAYOUT: exactly 6 frames in a 3 x 2 grid of equal cells (3 across, 2 down). Each cell is a tall portrait rectangle twice as high as it is wide. Read left to right, top to bottom (frame 1 top-left, frame 6 bottom-right). NO grid lines, NO borders, NO frame numbers, NO text. Every cell shows the same area a moment later. The point of impact sits ON the bottom edge of every cell, in its middle, at the same place in every cell; nothing at all is drawn below it. The cracks fan out upward and sideways from it only, like the upper half of a spider web.

THE ANIMATION:
- frame 1: one sharp, bright impact node with short razor-thin ice-white cracks reaching about 25% of the way up;
- frames 2-3: angular cracks race upward and branch, reaching about 55% and then 80% of the way up;
- frames 4-5: the cracks reach the cell's left, right and top edges, with hairline fractures between them and a faint pale-cyan and crimson glow along their edges;
- frame 6: the complete fracture web over the whole cell above the point of impact.
Each frame keeps every crack of the one before unchanged, in the same place, and adds new ones: frame 4 contains every crack of frame 3 unchanged plus new ones, and so on to frame 6. The cracks only grow.

Thin luminous fracture lines only, white-hot cores with a thin soft glow. No glass surface, no shading, no shards, no dust, no reflections, no objects, no text.

ring.prompt:
A sprite sheet for a game VFX artist: the frame-by-frame animation of ONE effect for a commercial PC rhythm game, at the finish level of a top commercial action game's hand-painted VFX flipbooks.

LAYOUT: exactly 16 frames in a 4 x 4 grid of equal square cells, read left to right, top to bottom (frame 1 top-left, frame 16 bottom-right). Pure black background (#000000) everywhere. NO grid lines, NO borders, NO frame numbers, NO text. The effect is centred on the same point in every cell and stays inside its cell with black space around it; nothing touches a cell edge.

THE EFFECT: the SHOCKWAVE of a heavy seal being stamped down at the centre of the cell, seen flat from the front. The seal itself is NOT drawn: only the ring of force and light that runs out from where it lands. Every element is white and grey light only, with no colour at all, because the game colours it itself.

THE ANIMATION, one continuous motion across the 16 frames:
- frames 1-2: a small blinding round flash at the centre with a thin bright ring just leaving it;
- frames 3-5: the ring is a thick, bright, perfectly circular shockwave running outward fast, with short radial streaks and specks of dust thrown ahead of it;
- frames 6-10: the ring has grown to most of the cell and is thinner, it breaks into separate arcs, a second, fainter, thinner ring follows it inside, and the specks fly on outward;
- frames 11-14: only thin broken arcs near the edge of the effect and a few specks are left, fading;
- frames 15-16: almost nothing, the last faint arc; frame 16 is black.

Every frame is a different drawing of the same event a moment later: shapes change, break up and travel outward, they are not one picture scaled up. Painterly, energetic, with sharp bright edges and soft glow. It is light only, on black, to be added onto the screen. No ground, no objects, no characters, no logos, no letters, no numbers.

sparks.prompt:
